  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Migration Resource Centers in Guatemala</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Large numbers of migrants, asylum seekers and refugees of different nationalities transit through Guatemala each year, at the same time as thousands of mostly young Guatemalans, especially indigenous people, emigrate to Mexico and the United States in search of opportunities abroad, often through irregular channels. The country also receives thousands of returnees each year. This proposed project responds to a complex situation in the country where few services exist to support the population. Through a network of two fixed (IOM), four mobile (UNHCR) and three field (2 IOM and 1 UNHCR) migrant reception centres, IOM and partners will provide support to mixed migration flows, through a comprehensive approach to service provisions and referrals where necessary. The project also contributes to a collaborative strategy in coordination with UNHCR, UNICEF and relevant ministries of the Government of Guatemala (GoG), focused on the implementation of programs, provision of services and enhancement of infrastructure that facilitate access to assistance, protection, and lawful immigration avenues for different profiles of populations, including potential migrants and people on the move in the context of mixed movements taking place in Central America.</narrative>
  </description>
